---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const title = "About";
const description =
  "Who runs this site, what it is for, how it is funded, and the limits of what " +
  "it does. Built and maintained by Tilak Chandra Shastri, AMFI-registered " +
  "mutual fund distributor (ARN-346031).";
---

<Base title={title} description={description} crumb="Reference / About">
  <h1>About this site</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A reference for Indian equity markets: standard technical indicators computed
    daily across the NSE universe, a screener you control the thresholds on, and
    written explanations of how the underlying concepts actually work.
  </p>

  <h2>Who runs it</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Tilak Chandra Shastri.</strong> I am an independent,
    <strong>AMFI-registered Mutual Fund Distributor</strong> —
    <span class="c">ARN-346031</span> — operating as
    <strong>Shastri Financial Services</strong>, with around five years of
    hands-on experience in the stock market.
  </p>
  <p>
    I built the analytics behind this site myself: the data pipeline, the
    indicator calculations, the backtesting engine and the screener. It began as
    a personal research project and this is the public, educational part of it.
  </p>

  <h2>Why it exists</h2>
  <p>
    Most Indian market content falls into one of two piles: tip services telling
    you what to buy, or theory with no data attached. I wanted the third thing —
    the actual numbers, computed transparently, with an honest explanation of
    what they do and do not tell you.
  </p>
  <p>
    That includes publishing the unflattering parts. A strategy's losing periods
    are more instructive than its winning ones, and a screen that looks selective
    is often just a threshold chosen after the fact. Where this site has
    something to say about that, it says it.
  </p>

  <h2>What it is not</h2>
  <div class="defs">
    <div class="def">
      <div class="h"><code>not_advisory</code><span class="meta">important</span></div>
      <p>This site does not provide personalised investment advice. It publishes
        computed values and explanations. Whether any security suits you depends
        on your goals, horizon and risk tolerance — none of which it knows.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="def">
      <div class="h"><code>not_a_tip_service</code><span class="meta">by design</span></div>
      <p>There are no buy or sell calls here, and no entry, stop-loss or target
        prices. You set the filters; the site reports what the data says.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="def">
      <div class="h"><code>separate_from_my_distribution_business</code><span class="meta">disclosure</span></div>
      <p>My mutual fund distribution business is a separate activity, conducted
        under ARN-346031 at
        <a href="https://tilak004.github.io/Business_website/" rel="noopener">Shastri
        Financial Services</a>. This site is not a sales channel for it, and
        nothing here is conditional on becoming a client.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>How the data is produced</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Daily OHLCV from public sources, indicators computed with standard published
    formulas, refreshed once per trading day. Where a value cannot be computed it
    is shown as unavailable rather than estimated, and every row carries the date
    of the price bar it came from. Full detail on the
    <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How it is funded</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Through advertising. Ads are kept away from controls and never placed to
    encourage accidental clicks. No content on this site is written to create ad
    inventory, and no advertiser has any influence over what it says.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Corrections, questions and disagreements are all welcome — particularly
    corrections. See the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
